# Modified by Shipwright, 2026: rebranded as Shoal Messages; Keel Actions; see CHANGES-FROM-UPSTREAM.md.
# D-Bus activation, so sharing works when Shoal Messages is not running.
#
# The name is not free: Sailjail derives it from the OrganizationName and
# ApplicationName in the desktop file, the same pair that decides where the
# app's data lives, and the share dialog looks the app up under exactly that
# name. Renaming it here would move the state store on the next start.
#
# Started through sailjail rather than the booster for the same reason the
# desktop file uses a generic application type: the Rust core's runtime does
# not survive being dlopened from a preforked process.
#
# Shipwright: it also starts the app for a Keel Actions call (Pilot, through
# keel-mcp) that finds it closed. Keel apps have a generated file of their own
# that starts them without a window (--keel-actions); this app cannot, the one
# name being spent here, so such a call opens Shoal Messages as a tap would.
[D-BUS Service]
Name=org.shipwright.ShoalMessages
Exec=/usr/bin/sailjail -p shipwright-shoal-messages.desktop /usr/bin/shipwright-shoal-messages
